# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Stream S23: .pyi parity sweep.
#
# ``from .tenzor_core import *`` in ``python/tenzor/__init__.py`` bulk-imports
# every pybind11 binding registered on the C++ extension. The block below
# enumerates the runtime surface so static checkers stop reporting
# ``module 'tenzor' has no attribute 'X'``. Signatures are deliberately
# minimal (``def foo(*args: Any, **kwargs: Any) -> Any: ...``) — full
# typing per-op is tracked separately. Adding the names is the load-bearing
# fix: it lets IDEs and mypy/pyright resolve the attributes.
#
# The check_pyi_parity.py drift checker (and its CTest entry
# ``cpu_python_test_pyi_drift``) keeps this list in sync.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

